WEBVTT

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.720
Even if something happened 40 years ago,

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.600
it shouldn't change the fact that he is a fear of darkness.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.390
He turned away from the fear and acted as if there was no memory of his own history.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:19.730
If I live here, my son who regained his memory may come to see me someday.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.670
I think so.

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:26.160
What I lived here is left in the resident record.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:28.260
It's okay to move.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:30.710
Don't worry about it.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:35.320
Keep a close eye on Kigitsumada.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:36.200
Hmm.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.740
Negotiator.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:39.760
You should be done.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.480
It's about a new job.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.860
My parent company wants you to work for them.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:50.170
Your parent company?

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.480
Whether it's a bakery, a real estate company, or even the military police.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:10.160
If you say it's a parent company in this city, it's definitely in the same place.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:17.590
This city is the god of a company called Paradigm.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:55.400
Roger Smith-san, I am Phil Gazze, the publisher of Paradigm Press.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.520
It's not your first time meeting him, is it?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.320
Patricia Lovejoy.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:15.120
The name I asked before was Miss Casey, wasn't it?

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:29.200
Angel.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:31.670
I told you to call me that, didn't I?

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:06.980
I was disappointed at your boring request.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.190
Since when have you been working here?

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:11.800
A week ago.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.900
What are you aiming for?

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:14.900
Aim?

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.050
I'm just a woman.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:25.960
Alex Rosewater.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:32.020
That's the essence of Paradigm.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:39.440
Can we live by breaking past memories?

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:45.000
When and where does the accident happen?

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.780
Where does it lead us?

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:57.350
Paradigm Press reporter Michael Zebacher has been asked to...

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:59.970
The article he interviewed was published by Kogane.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.050
It was a negotiation to make Paradigm go to Paradigm in exchange for the retirement fund.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:11.470
The job itself is not difficult. There are two problems.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:15.810
I'm wondering if I should take a job in a department close to Paradigm headquarters.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:23.930
And most of all, the Zebacha has disappeared three months ago.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.880
You've even started to take on a job like a detective.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:34.620
Mr. Negotiator.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:37.820
There are only two ways for a person who quit the police.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:45.300
Either become a private detective and look into other people's lives,

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:49.670
or destroy other people's lives with illegal broadcasting organizations.

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:51.050
I just want the information of the negotiator.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:57.590
It's been a long time since I came back to Flos, so I just got nostalgic.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:06:59.420
Roger Smith.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.720
Michael Zeebacher, a German.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:09.160
He hasn't made any inquiries.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.360
He hasn't been paid for two months.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:14.090
Is he no longer in this town?

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:15.010
No.

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:19.280
It's impossible for a person who lived inside the dome to go outside.

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:21.790
I see.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:24.630
Roger.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.300
It seems that the missing journalist was a double-living person.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:41.360
He's renting an apartment there except for his wife and class.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:50.440
You left here because you hated it, but we are proud of the military police.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.340
I thank you for this matter, Dustin.

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:21.630
I've lived my life as a journalist.

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:27.120
I write articles about the truth.

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:34.750
However, in this city, the truth is not something that can be touched by a newspaper reporter.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:45.090
And the truth that you really have to know is that no one in this city wants to know it.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.140
What you have to know.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:54.660
What you have to know.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.980
That's...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:27.600
That's it.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.560
The dog is rotten!

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.810
Michael Zebacher!

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:37.740
Michael Zebacher has already disappeared from this world.

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:41.050
Tell your owner that!

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:46.830
Then what is your name?

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:49.220
Should I call you Schwarzbart?

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.290
Black Forest?

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:54.120
Report to your owner!

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:56.800
Don't worry anymore!

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:59.640
The poor newspaper reporter will never...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.300
You have to show up in this town!

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:02.420
Hahahaha!

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:17.520
I will dig up the truth.

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:21.530
Aren't you cold?

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:27.360
Oh, are you taking care of my health?

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:29.270
Not really.

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:35.700
Androids and Megadeus exist in this world in advance.

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:39.070
People have no doubt about that.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:42.740
But don't they just think that's the way it is?

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:49.570
Dorothy, have you ever thought about why you're moving?

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.970
I'm thinking about myself more than you are.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:58.550
This is about yourself.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:02.350
It seems that a time has come when I have to face the darkness within myself.

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:23.020
In order to transport the Big O, I am using this underground tunnel.

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:28.760
It seems that a transporter called Subway was once installed here.

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.630
Even if it's just 30 feet below the ground,

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:38.760
there's no one who wants to come here, not even a bank robber.

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:44.920
Big Ear said this 40 years ago.

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:47.340
People have lived in this basement before.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:52.660
I've never come down from here either.

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:56.360
It's probably a world that no one in this city knows.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:59.870
Just one person.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:08.390
The wall has become a new thing.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.840
The deeper it is, the more new things are buried.

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:28.170
I'm scared.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:30.500
I'm scared.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:38.040
What is it that makes you feel this indescribable emotion?

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:47.680
I have no choice but to respond.

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:50.500
You should be able to overcome it with reason.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:54.430
This is an absurd emotion.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:03.080
Ma

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:25.960
Oh

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:30.790
There is, Dorothy!

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.290
Ma, the mother?

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:34.440
You mean your mother?

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:36.570
That doesn't matter!

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:38.030
It has nothing to do with you!

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.410
That's not what I mean!

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.270
Why are you here?

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:44.730
Roger's physiological response is back to normal.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:45.270
What?

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:57.330
Dorothy, do you want to know too?

00:13:57.590 --> 00:13:59.320
Do you have any fear?

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:07.230
I don't know how you feel, but even my father doesn't know why I'm thinking.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:25.930
Dr. Wainwright is the first in the android research.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:29.490
The father of the craftsman

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.800
Then you're the best craftsman I've ever seen.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:34.730
I didn't understand all the core technologies.

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:38.920
I just built myself up to reproduce my dead daughter.

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:46.120
There's no one in this world who knows everything.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:50.140
But if something is scaring you,

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:53.000
there are people who turn a blind eye to it,

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.920
and there are people who try to overcome it by seeing through it.

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:59.850
Humans are the same.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.430
It's not like that. Each person is a different being.

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:04.200
R. Doroshii

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:07.190
Doroshii

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:08.570
Oto

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.480
It's a big deal for a dog from Paradigm.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:07.780
Eber! No, Schwartzwald! What are you doing here?

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:12.060
Big Archetype?

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:18.610
40 years ago, something happened and we lost our memories.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:22.450
How much power did people have until then?

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.380
Is this power?

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:29.840
Megadeus wasn't special, Nego Shin.

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:35.980
Even I, if I can get my memory back, I can obtain this power.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:39.460
Is this still working?

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:41.460
It was buried here.

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:43.490
I removed that lock.

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:46.620
Thanks to you, I became like this.

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:51.580
I wish you were in the same shape as me at that time.

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:03.650
lol

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:14.920
Droid!

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:25.410
What are you doing!

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:42.500
What happened? Why is this moving?

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:53.070
What should I do?

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:56.960
He's alive.

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:59.290
My information...

00:18:15.964 --> 00:18:16.964
Bye.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.900
I heard they're aiming at Dorothy.

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:46.170
Please wait a moment.

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:59.660
This is my, my friend.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:03.400
I don't know where he came from.

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:08.400
That's something I can't say.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:44.830
Kill him!

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.160
You don't have to be scared.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:56.520
I didn't think you'd go under the subway.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:00.920
Defeat the ghost!

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:18.050
I don't know who you are or where you're from, but at least you're not a god!

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.080
You're stronger than Zeus.

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:05.370
I can't.

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:09.190
What are you doing? Look closely.

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:11.660
That's a monster that has nothing to do with you.

00:21:12.280 --> 00:21:17.040
Big-O, I'm not your friend.

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.630
I won't hold back.

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:03.090
He's definitely an excellent negotiator.

00:22:03.470 --> 00:22:11.770
Aren't you cold?

00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:14.010
What's that?

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:15.680
It's like a greeting.

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:16.870
I can even sense the temperature.

00:22:18.110 --> 00:22:27.940
It's an unbearable android.

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:38.060
At this time I lost the river

00:23:41.150 --> 00:23:48.230
I felt it is so much a man

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:52.380
Someone

00:24:00.572 --> 00:24:02.292
We'll be together now.

